Hi!

I was wondering what the stopping rule is for convergence = "auto" with target = "jags".

I tried to inspect the source code but it was not immediately clear to me:
https://github.com/ecmerkle/blavaan/blob/master/R/blavaan.R

I see that for autorun.jags() there is a max.time parameter that needs to be set, but the documentation for blavaan did not mention whether it should be set manually by the call to blavaan() or whether it is set to a default value by blavaan() - as far as I could see.

I currently have a two models that have been fitting for 1.5 day with convergence = "auto", so I am curious when (and whether) the process will stop by itself :)

Thanks in advance!

Best,
Niels

