Niels,

I believe this is using the default from autorun.jags(), which is Inf. So I do not think it will stop by itself.

It has been awhile since I looked at it, but I can remember instances where one chain gets stuck near 0 or diverges off to large values, so that convergence is never achieved (at least, not in the time that I want to wait!).

You should be able to change max.time using the bcontrol argument in blavaan, e.g.,

bcontrol = list(max.time = "5hours")

Ed

