Warning messages:
1:
40 (1.3%) p_waic estimates greater than 0.4. We recommend trying loo instead.
2: Some Pareto k diagnostic values are slightly high. See help('pareto-k-diagnostic') for details.

3:
17 (0.5%) p_waic estimates greater than 0.4. We recommend trying loo instead.

Can you please explain in more detail what I need to do?

31 Ocak 2023 Salı tarihinde saat 07:20:45 UTC+3 itibarıyla Ed Merkle şunları yazdı:

> That is a warning message, as opposed to an error, so the function worked but it alerted you that there might be a problem with the results. In this case, if it only gives a warning for p_waic and not for p_loo, then you could use the looic instead of waic. (This all assumes that you are using fitMeasures().)
>
> That warning actually comes from the loo package, which blavaan uses to compute waic and looic. For more detail about what that warning means, see:
>
> https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/loo/vignettes/loo2-example.html
>
> Ed
>
>
